# What a generator writes, marked so git stops printing it as a patch.
#
# EVERY RULE HERE IS KEYED TO A FILE A SCRIPT CUTS. What a person types keeps its diff;
# what a script writes does not, because nobody reads that patch and every reader pays
# for it — `git show` on a commit that moved the enclosure and the port rings emitted
# 128 MB to carry a few kilobytes of Python. A rule keyed wider than its generator's
# output would swallow a diff somebody wanted, so the drawings below are named by the
# directory their generator writes into rather than by suffix, and the hand-drawn SVGs
# beside them keep theirs.
#
# `-diff` IS THE WHOLE OF WHAT IT DOES. The bytes are untouched, `git grep` still reads
# them, the working tree holds the same file it always held, and `git diff` says the two
# differ instead of showing how. `linguist-generated` is that same claim made to GitHub,
# which collapses these in a compare view and leaves them out of the language bar.
#
# What is NOT here is as deliberate. A scorecard sidecar is twelve hundred lines and its
# gate rows are worth reading; ios/AppIcon.svg and tools/anim_frames/*.svg are small and
# hand-shaped. They diff.

# STEP IS ASCII, and a solid is hundreds of kilobytes of it. Three are in the index — the elbow,
# the tee and the y-divider, harvested solids with no builder here. The geometry is read by
# loading it; a reader who wants to know what moved opens the part, never the patch.
#
# The generated solids are in no index. hardware/cad-artifacts.lock.json names them and the
# release asset they arrive in, and web/scripts/fetch-cad-artifacts.mjs puts them on the disk.
*.step  -diff linguist-generated=true

# GIT DOES NOT DETECT THESE AS BINARY. A card deck's PDF carries no NUL byte inside the
# first 8000, which is the whole of what the heuristic looks at, so deck.pdf (42 MB) and
# deck-tools.pdf (17 MB) go out as patch text — 73 MB of the 128 MB above. `binary` is
# `-diff -merge -text`, and the last of those says the file is not to be line-ending
# converted, which is true of a PDF and has never been stated here.
*.pdf  binary linguist-generated=true

# The board's renders are ONE LINE EACH, half a megabyte to nine hundred kilobytes of it.
# A single character moving in the silk prints the whole file twice — the commit that set
# the silk's own commit hash cost 8.4 MB to carry ten lines. Keyed to the out/ directory
# every board renders into, so the carrier is covered by the same rule as the pcba.
hardware/pcb/*/out/*.svg  -diff linguist-generated=true

# Blender Freestyle stroke soup, cut by the _blender_render.py sitting beside it.
hardware/**/drawings/line-art/*.svg  -diff linguist-generated=true

# gen_animation_frames.py, sixteen 360x360 frames as RGB565 hex, 28 MB of it. Keyed to the
# images directory rather than to *.h, because every other header under firmware/ is typed.
firmware/src_front/images/anim_*.h  -diff linguist-generated=true
